rac{1}{2})$ and $y(1)$ rounded to $2$ decimal places.$y(\\frac{1}{2}) \\approx$ {{field-1}},\n$y(1) \\approx$ {{field-2}}" 13194139535003 false] [17592186221948 1145 "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,{y}_{0}=y({x}_{0}),\n$$\n\nthe implicit Euler method with step size $Δx$ is given by\n\n$$\nΔy={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwith ${y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}=f({x}_{\\text{new}},{y}_{\\text{new}})$ evaluated at the next $x$ and $y$ values.\n\nFirst, note that we are given $y(0)$ and asked to find $y(1).$ The distance from $x=0$ to $x=1$ is $1,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{1-0}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =(2{x}_{\\text{new}}-3{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{x}_{\\text{new}}-\\frac{3}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2(y+{x}_{\\text{new}})}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(1).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2(y+{x}_{\\text{new}})}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1+\\frac{1}{2})}{5} \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2},\\,y=0.6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2(y+{x}_{\\text{new}})}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(0.6+1)}{5} \\\\  & =0.64.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\ny(\\frac{1}{2})≈0.60,\\,y(1)≈0.64.\n$$" 13194139535003 true] [17592186325993 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325994 13194139535003 true] [17592186325993 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325995 13194139535003 true] [17592186325993 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325996 13194139535003 true] [17592186325993 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325997 13194139535003 true] [17592186325993 1000 #edb/ref 17592186325998 13194139535003 true] [17592186325993 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535003 true] [17592186325993 1041 "selection" 13194139535003 true] [17592186325993 1104 #edb/ref 17592186325997 13194139535003 true] [17592186325993 1110 #uuid "23d59c99-8926-55b2-a5b5-70b2e7823ff4" 13194139535003 true] [17592186325994 1034 "{y}_{\\text{new}}=y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3y" 13194139535003 true] [17592186325994 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535003 true] [17592186325994 1111 #uuid "4fd4410d-6096-5268-bc63-d77015ce9b4b" 13194139535003 true] [17592186325995 1034 "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}{1+3y}" 13194139535003 true] [17592186325995 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535003 true] [17592186325995 1111 #uuid "3d0d76d4-fdf0-5c58-8640-57094a8e0d3f" 13194139535003 true] [17592186325996 1034 "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}{1-3{x}_{\\text{new}}}" 13194139535003 true] [17592186325996 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535003 true] [17592186325996 1111 #uuid "d1c506b0-1af0-5d4f-9700-aed86aa76ce0" 13194139535003 true] [17592186325997 1034 "{y}_{\\text{new}}=\\frac{y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}}{1+3{x}_{\\text{new}}}" 13194139535003 true] [17592186325997 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535003 true] [17592186325997 1111 #uuid "c366c38a-ffcd-5bb4-b2a0-e080c13b9488" 13194139535003 true] [17592186325998 1034 "{y}_{\\text{new}}=y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}-3{x}_{\\text{new}}y" 13194139535003 true] [