t{new}} & =y-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y-{x}_{\\text{new}}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(-\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(0).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=-1,\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=-1+\\frac{1}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y-{x}_{\\text{new}}}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1-(-\\frac{1}{2})}{5} \\\\  & =0.50.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{1}{2},\\,y=0.5.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=0.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2\\cdot y-{x}_{\\text{new}}}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 0.5-0}{5} \\\\  & =0.20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\ny(-\\frac{1}{2})≈0.50,\\,y(0)≈0.20.\n$$" 13194139535003 true] [17592186326052 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326053 13194139535003 true] [17592186326052 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326054 13194139535003 true] [17592186326052 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326055 13194139535003 true] [17592186326052 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535003 true] [17592186326052 1041 "field-1" 13194139535003 true] [17592186326052 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326054 13194139535003 true] [17592186326052 1110 #uuid "7a9ff7a3-69ab-5583-a2f7-cce9862de625" 13194139535003 true] [17592186326053 1034 "0.40" 13194139535003 true] [17592186326053 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535003 true] [17592186326053 1111 #uuid "f7e75089-0d73-5b3e-bf31-5122bfadcecf" 13194139535003 true] [17592186326054 1034 "0.50" 13194139535003 true] [17592186326054 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535003 true] [17592186326054 1111 #uuid "a8bbc796-9cb2-5c5f-930a-feaf2befcff4" 13194139535003 true] [17592186326055 1034 "1.50" 13194139535003 true] [17592186326055 1103 #edb/ref 1759218604