w}})^{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ (1+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}){y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}(({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1) \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}(2y+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1)}{1+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1}{2+2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(1).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1}{2+2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+1}{2+2{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =1.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2},\\,y=1.3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =\\frac{2y+({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}+1}{2+2({x}_{\\text{new}})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 1.3+{1}^{2}+1}{2+2({1}^{2})} \\\\  & =1.15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that \n\n$$\ny(\\frac{1}{2})≈1.30,\\,y(1)≈1.15.\n$$" 13194139535003 true] [17592186326070 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326071 13194139535003 true] [17592186326070 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326072 13194139535003 true] [17592186326070 1000 #edb/ref 17592186326073 13194139535003 true] [17592186326070 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045451 13194139535003 true] [17592186326070 1041 "field-1" 13194139535003 true] [17592186326070 1104 #edb/ref 17592186326072 13194139535003 true] [17592186326070 1110 #uuid "b93524ca-c3a0-5702-a487-5b79800baab9" 13194139535003 true] [17592186326071 1034 "1.20" 13194139535003 true] [17592186326071 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535003 true] [17592186326071 1111 #uuid "e102d97e-ad41-5e05-9f03-67896a5930ba" 131941